{"name":"Flare Gun","hex":"#ff4519","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flare gun","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large-bore pistol-like firearm used to fire signal flares."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flare_gun"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flare gun","blocks":[{"text":"A flare gun, also known as a Very pistol (sometimes spelled Verey) or signal pistol, is a large-bore handgun that discharges flares, blanks and smoke. Today, a flare gun is typically used to produce a distress signal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Single_shot%2C12_Gauge%2C_flare_gun.jpg/330px-Single_shot%2C12_Gauge%2C_flare_gun.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flare_gun"},{"title":"Flare","blocks":[{"text":"A flare is a type of pyrotechnic that produces a bright light or intense heat without an explosion. Flares are used for distress signaling, illumination, or defensive countermeasures in civilian and military applications. Flares may be ground pyrotechnics, projectile pyrotechnics, or parachute-suspended to provide maximum illumination time over a large area. Projectile pyrotechnics may be dropped from aircraft, fired from rocket or artillery, or deployed by flare guns or handheld percussive tubes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/US_Army_52253_Best_Warrior_At_Night.jpg/330px-US_Army_52253_Best_Warrior_At_Night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flare"},{"title":"Gun","blocks":[{"text":"A gun is a device that propels a projectile using pressure or explosive force. The projectiles are typically solid, but can also be pressurized liquid, or gas. Solid projectiles may be free-flying or tethered. A large-caliber gun is also called a cannon, while a hand-held gun may be called a firearm. Guns were designed as weapons for military use, and then found use in hunting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/SIG_Pro_by_Augustas_Didzgalvis.jpg/330px-SIG_Pro_by_Augustas_Didzgalvis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gun"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Single_shot%2C12_Gauge%2C_flare_gun.jpg/500px-Single_shot%2C12_Gauge%2C_flare_gun.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Single_shot%2C12_Gauge%2C_flare_gun.jpg/500px-Single_shot%2C12_Gauge%2C_flare_gun.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Orion-brand single-shot, breech-loaded, 12 gauge flare gun. Its design is typical of commercially available flare guns, with a high-visibility red casing.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASingle_shot%2C12_Gauge%2C_flare_gun.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/26.5mm_Flare_Gun.jpg/500px-26.5mm_Flare_Gun.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/26.5mm_Flare_Gun.jpg/1280px-26.5mm_Flare_Gun.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/26.5mm_Flare_Gun.jpg/500px-26.5mm_Flare_Gun.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A single-shot, 26.5/25 mm flare gun manufactured by Patel Ballistics. It is chambered in a different caliber from the Orion flare gun.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A26.5mm_Flare_Gun.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Webley_%26_Scott_Mk_III_flare_pistol.jpg/500px-Webley_%26_Scott_Mk_III_flare_pistol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1